{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshReuseResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RefreshReuseResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"RefreshReuseResponse","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK20RefreshReuseResponseO"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshReuseResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"revoke_session"},{"type":"text","text":" — the default (D-N2). The refusal also invalidates the session the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replayed token names (which publishes to the revocation feed) and revokes every refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token issued under that session — whichever client it was issued to, the console sign-in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, with no back-channel logout sent — as the authorization-code replay path does for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a code (RFC 6749 §10.5; OAuth 2.0 Security BCP §4.14.2). Only a presentation by the token’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own client, passing the token’s sender constraint, triggers it (#821). On a client with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grace window the honest holder of a replayed token has nothing left to lose — its token is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already dead and it never received the successor — so the revocation costs it nothing and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs whoever holds the successor everything. * "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse"},{"type":"text","text":" — the 1.1.x behaviour: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"presentation is refused, marked on the session and audited, and nothing else is revoked."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Neither value changes what is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"accepted","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fapi2"},{"type":"text","text":" client’s presentation inside the grace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window is accepted and marked whatever this says (D-N4); a token revoked at logout is not a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replay and revokes nothing. This text is published as the schema’s description in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdks\/openapi.json"},{"type":"text","text":", so it carries no rustdoc intra-doc links (F4-W1-08, #824)."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including the records the caller did ask for.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"access. ","type":"text"},{"code":".u